{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794169487,"nonce":"mfpqJcMGqaogifDc3s0P2IVEC9A=","message":"Cause found: text elements carried letter-spacing in points while the font size was scaled to device pixels, so at 3x the cn input's -0.35 spacing was drawn as -0.35 px per glyph instead of -1.05 px. The drawn run grew 0.23 pt per character wider than the caret's measurement; after '你好 hello w' the caret (measured 66.58 pt) sat 2.33 pt inside the drawn 'w' (68.91 pt). Not specific to Pinyin: any letter-spaced text at 2x or 3x. Fix in node_content.rs scales letter-spacing like the font size; on the iPhone the drawn run is now 66.58 pt, matching the caret. Test: text_spacing_tests::letter_spacing_scales_with_the_font_at_device_density. Uncommitted, awaiting the owner's check.","files":null}]}